seg-7d2165f7b65c = IMO guidance on GNSS interference for ships: what Kshana supports evidence for

# text
seg-37fe70c1c7cc = IMO's GNSS-interference text for ships is thin: MSC.1/Circ.1644 is addressed mainly to Member States, and the ship-side expectations sit in the radionavigation system resolution and the multi-system receiver performance standard. This file maps those three documents. No IMO circular on GNSS interference later than MSC.1/Circ.1644 was found; check the IMO document library for newer ones.

# text
# c1: kshana compliance-report
seg-ff0e00610721 = Every row says which Kshana outputs <b>support evidence for</b> the requirement and what is left over. Nothing here says a framework is met or that any product has been rated or approved by anyone. Run <c1/> on your own result files to see which rows your runs actually evidence; see <a1>README.md</a1>.

